spacing out. And how does that relate to the learning experience you just had? And she used brain decoding and got this really cool result. It sort of makes sense that the concepts that people struggled with the most when they were trying to learn this new thing that she was teaching them about were the ones that appeared the most on their sort of mental playlist when they were spacing out, right? Which is very adaptive, right? You don't want to spend your time thinking about stuff you already know. You want to spend your time working through the stuff that you don't know very well, And she was able to get a very tangible clear evidence for this idea using brain decoding. Let me ask you a long-term question, which is whether the goal is some kind of a universal thought decoder so that there'll be an absolute lexicon of what we know thoughts consist of.
走神时，播放列表上有什么。这与你刚刚经历的学习体验有什么关系？她使用了大脑解码，并得到了这个非常酷的结果。人们在试图学习她所教的新事物时最挣扎的概念，正是那些在他们走神时出现在他们心理播放列表上最多的概念，这非常有适应性。你不想把时间花在思考你已经知道的事情上。你想把时间花在解决那些你掌握得不好的事情上。她利用大脑解码为这个想法提供了非常具体、清晰的证据。让我问你一个长期的问题，即目标是否是某种通用的思想解码器，以便我们对思想的构成有一个绝对的词典。

