00:32:14.000 --> 00:32:58.000
And you can make a decoder, you know, for each one of those questions. And then we can do that now. And that's a universal thought decoder. But it doesn't work anywhere near perfectly. It's like a very blurry thought decoder. We can tell where your thoughts fit in like this 300-dimensional space. But there's like a huge cloud of uncertainty around our estimate of what you're thinking about, right? And with functional MRI, that has to do with just intrinsic limits on the resolution of the technique.
你可以为每一个问题制作一个解码器。我们现在就可以做到这一点，这就是一个通用的思维解码器。但它远未达到完美，就像一个非常模糊的思维解码器。我们可以判断你的想法在 300 维空间中的位置，但我们对你所想内容的估计周围存在巨大的不确定性。对于功能性磁共振成像（fMRI）来说，这与该技术分辨率的内在局限性有关。

